### Example: JSON Escaping Without sed/awk

Instead of:
```bash
escaped=$(echo "$content" | sed 's/\\/\\\\/g' | sed 's/"/\\"/g' | awk '{printf "%s\\n", $0}')
```

Use pure bash:
```bash
escape_for_json() {
    local input="$1"
    local output=""
    local i char
    for (( i=0; i<${#input}; i++ )); do
        char="${input:$i:1}"
        case "$char" in
            $'\\') output+='\\' ;;
            '"') output+='\"' ;;
            $'\n') output+='\n' ;;
            $'\r') output+='\r' ;;
            $'\t') output+='\t' ;;
            *) output+="$char" ;;
        esac
    done
    printf '%s' "$output"
}
```

